{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"03b5cbde-262b-4f9f-ad31-08c8a8be14a5","update":{"sessionUpdate":"available_commands_update","availableCommands":[{"name":"goal","description":"Run until the specified goal is completely finished."},{"name":"compact","description":"Compact the conversation now (summarize history to free up the context window)."},{"name":"schedule","description":"Run an instruction on a recurring schedule or as a one-time timer."},{"name":"browser","description":"Invoke a browser agent for web tasks."},{"name":"plan","description":"Plan carefully before executing a task."},{"name":"grill-me","description":"Interview me to align on a plan."},{"name":"teamwork","description":"Invoke a team of agents to autonomously tackle large projects."},{"name":"learn","description":"Reflect on recent successes or corrections to capture reusable skills or rules."},{"name":"boost","description":"Invoke the Boost multi-agent orchestrator for complex tasks."},{"name":"agy-customizations","description":"Comprehensive guide and reference for the Antigravity Customization System. Use to explain how customizations work, their loading priority, discovery mechanisms, and to guide the creation of skills, rules, plugins, hooks, and MCP servers."},{"name":"antigravity-guide","description":"Provides a comprehensive guide, quick reference, and sitemap for Google Antigravity (AGY), including the Antigravity CLI (agy), Antigravity 2.0, Antigravity IDE, Python SDK, slash commands, keybindings, and customizations (skills, rules, MCP, sidecars). Activate this skill when the user asks questions about how to use, configure, or customize Antigravity, AGY, the agy CLI, the Antigravity IDE, or Antigravity 2.0."},{"name":"dataframe-column-modification-policy","description":"Mandatory rule to never arbitrarily add or delete DataFrame columns without explicit user permission. Always activate this skill when processing, modifying, analyzing, or cleaning tabular/DataFrame data."},{"name":"git-commit-strategy","description":"Always use this skill when preparing, staging, and committing changes in Git repositories to enforce atomic commits, logical change separation, and structured commit messages."},{"name":"implementation-plan-tool-specification","description":"Always use this skill when drafting, creating, or updating implementation plans (*_Plan.md, *_PLAN.md) to explicitly specify libraries, modules, frameworks, and tools used for every feature."},{"name":"korean-terminal-encoding","description":"Always use this skill when executing terminal commands, running Python scripts, printing logs, reading/writing files, or plotting charts with Korean text on Windows to ensure UTF-8 encoding and prevent character corruption (한글 깨짐 방지)."},{"name":"openai-default-model","description":"OpenAI 모델이나 API를 사용할 때 기본 모델로 항상 gpt-6-luna를 적용하는 전역 스킬입니다. Use whenever configuring, setting environment variables, writing code, or invoking OpenAI models."},{"name":"reverse-engineer-anything","description":"Reverse engineer native, managed, Electron/JavaScript, packaged, firmware, and browser targets with REA. Use shipped-artifact or requested runtime evidence to explain features, compare versions, decompile code, or guide a reconstruction. Skip REA for ordinary source-repository architecture analysis."},{"name":"uv-package-management","description":"Always use this skill when installing, adding, managing, updating, or removing Python packages and libraries across any Python workspace or project."}]}}}
